{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK6QoijMkKT7kG4YQQRD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`HttpResponse(memoryview(b\"My Content\")).content` now returns `b'My Content'`. The `httpwrappers` and `responses` test suites pass.\n\nThere were two problems in `django/http/response.py`, and both needed a change:\n- **The content setter** checks whether a value can be iterated over and joins the pieces. A memoryview can be iterated over, so it was being taken apart byte by byte instead of handled as one value. It's now treated like `bytes` and `str` and passed through whole.\n- **`make_bytes`** only turned `bytes` directly into the output. Anything else, including a memoryview, went through `str()`, which is where `b'<memory at 0x...>'` came from. It now turns a memoryview straight into bytes with `bytes(value)`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":19032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":609},"output_tokens":253,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88fe9a66-2748-4083-8db3-06dabe1ef88e","uuid":"28ba4c1a-c5cd-45dc-b5c9-c297df87b47d","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:46:03.077Z","request_id":"req_011ChK6QoYocZEGjkQbjhK3P"}
